WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.918
Write Postgres extensions

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.720
in plain Go

00:00:03.246 --> 00:00:05.368
gopgext builds PostgreSQL

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.771
extensions from ordinary

00:00:06.583 --> 00:00:07.668
Go code using

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:08.293
TinyGo

00:00:08.432 --> 00:00:09.446
Mark a function

00:00:09.257 --> 00:00:10.082
with a comment

00:00:09.894 --> 00:00:11.049
directive and it

00:00:10.861 --> 00:00:11.922
becomes a SQL

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:12.464
function

00:00:13.006 --> 00:00:13.737
It writes the

00:00:13.548 --> 00:00:14.279
C glue

00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:15.447
the install script

00:00:15.364 --> 00:00:16.237
and the control

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:16.956
file for you

00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:17.779
Much of the

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.123
standard library works

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:20.680
and strings arrays

00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:21.529
timestamps

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.380
UUIDs and JSON

00:00:23.204 --> 00:00:24.147
map to SQL

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:24.677
types

00:00:25.214 --> 00:00:26.216
The author warns

00:00:26.051 --> 00:00:27.442
it is experimental

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:28.421
a bug runs

00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:29.459
inside the database

00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:30.237
server where it

00:00:30.049 --> 00:00:31.027
can crash it

00:00:30.886 --> 00:00:32.077
or corrupt data

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.612
Full story on

00:00:33.423 --> 00:00:34.319
the dashboard
